{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeProductSurjective","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeProductSurjective","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.PiBlockSeparation","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalInequivalence","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRangeTop","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedPartitionShape"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.heckeProduct_surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.heckeProduct_surjective","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeProductSurjective.lean#L132-L138","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.heckeProduct_range_eq_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.heckeProduct_range_eq_top","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeProductSurjective.lean#L113-L130","doc":"**`Φ` is surjective.**  Separation gives the block idempotents, `seminormalRep_range_eq_top`\ngives the entries, and `eq_top_of_separating_of_blockSurj` puts them together — with no density\ntheorem anywhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.contentPowSum_separates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.contentPowSum_separates","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeProductSurjective.lean#L100-L111","doc":"**The block scalars separate the partitions.**  Contrapositive of\n`youngDiagram_eq_of_contentPowSum_eq`, plus injectivity of `partitionShape`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.heckeProduct_jmPowSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.heckeProduct_jmPowSum","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeProductSurjective.lean#L89-L98","doc":"**The central Murphy power sums land on scalar tuples.**  Block `λ` sees the scalar\n`Σ_{c ∈ λ} (q^{2c})^m`, which is what `PiBlockSeparation` consumes as its separating family. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.heckeProduct_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.heckeProduct_apply","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeProductSurjective.lean#L84-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.heckeProduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.heckeProduct","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeProductSurjective.lean#L77-L82","doc":"**The block product map** `Φ = ⊕_λ ρ_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.partitionShape_card_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.partitionShape_card_succ","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeProductSurjective.lean#L72-L75","doc":"Every partition of `n+1` has a shape with `n+1` cells — the hypothesis `seminormalRep` wants. ","signatureChunk":0}]}